{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "33d2b301",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# New features by example\n",
    "\n",
    "The World Bank ModelFlow book uses **version 2.58**. This chapter shows the\n",
    "main changes since then, each with an example on the Pakistan model\n",
    "(`pak.pcim`) and a carbon tax scenario. The complete list, with the version\n",
    "where each change first shipped, is in\n",
    "[All changes since the book](changes_since_book.md). Installation is\n",
    "described in [Installing ModelFlow](installing.md).\n",
    "\n",
    "| Area | What is new | Section | Details |\n",
    "|---|---|---|---|\n",
    "| Saving models | `.pcimz` fast format for large models, `.pcims` structure only files, file names not case sensitive | [Saving and loading models](#saving) | [Model files](#changes-files) |\n",
    "| Reports | `model.table(scenarios=...)` makes tables of saved scenarios | [Tables with scenarios](#tables) | [Reporting](#changes-reporting) |\n",
    "| Solvers | next generation `_ng` solvers, including `newton_fbmin_ng`, which solves fast on the feedback set; `newton_implicit` fixed | [New solvers](#solvers) | [`_ng` solvers](#changes-ng) |\n",
    "| Graphs | drawing without graphviz (`engine='svg'`), interactive `model.causality()` | [Graphs without graphviz](#graphs) | [Drawing](#changes-drawing) |\n",
    "| Notebooks | Jupyter Notebook 7 / JupyterLab 4, MyST and mermaid in markdown cells, `model.plain_html` for RISE slides | [Jupyter 7 and JupyterLab](#jupyter) | [Packaging and notebooks](#changes-packaging) |\n",
    "| Input widgets | `%of` slider operators (percent of GDP), the same widget definitions in Shiny web apps | [Input widgets](#widgets) | [Widgets and apps](#changes-widgets) |\n",
    "| Large models | `factorizer=` (PARDISO, normal equations, MUMPS) for stacked systems too large for SuperLU, `straight=True` loading, stored derivatives | [Large models](#largemodels) | [`_ng` solvers](#changes-ng) |\n",
    "| Estimation | `af_level_df`: actual, fitted and residuals of the variable itself when the equation is estimated in `DLOG(CON)` or another transformation | [Fitted values](#fitted) | [Estimators](#changes-estimators) |\n",
    "| Differential equations | `modelode`: laws of motion written as `<ODE>` equations become Runge-Kutta steps; N-body helpers | [Differential equations](#ode) | [ODE models](#changes-ode) |\n",
    "| Monte Carlo | `modelmontecarlo`: stochastic simulation with fan charts, probabilities and parallel runs (not released yet) | [Monte Carlo simulation](#montecarlo) | |\n",
    "| Claude | plugins with skills for Claude Code and an MCP server which lets Claude load and run models | [ModelFlow with Claude](#claude) | |\n",
    "| Browser | ModelFlow runs in JupyterLite (Pyodide) without numba, graphviz or pyarrow | [Other changes](#other) | [Cloud and browser](#changes-deployment) |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "60261cf1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Setup\n",
    "\n",
    "The first cell installs ModelFlow when the notebook runs in Colab or in the\n",
    "browser (JupyterLite). On your own PC it does nothing. It also downloads the\n",
    "model file into the `data` folder if it is missing."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "5bafcb19",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "remove-cell"
    ]
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "import importlib.util\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "PAK_URL = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/IbHansen/modelflow-manual/main/model_repo/pak.pcim'\n",
    "\n",
    "if 'google.colab' in str(get_ipython()):\n",
    "    if importlib.util.find_spec(\"modelclass\") is None:\n",
    "        !apt-get -qq install -y graphviz\n",
    "        !pip -qq install ModelFlowIb > /dev/null 2>&1\n",
    "\n",
    "if sys.platform == 'emscripten':  # in the browser: JupyterLite\n",
    "    import micropip\n",
    "    await micropip.install('modelflowib>=2.86')\n",
    "    from pyodide.http import pyfetch\n",
    "    if not Path('data/pak.pcim').exists():\n",
    "        Path('data').mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n",
    "        response = await pyfetch(PAK_URL)\n",
    "        Path('data/pak.pcim').write_bytes(await response.bytes())\n",
    "elif not Path('data/pak.pcim').exists():\n",
    "    import urllib.request\n",
    "    Path('data').mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n",
    "    urllib.request.urlretrieve(PAK_URL, 'data/pak.pcim')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "ea11e792",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
