    "from modelclass import model\n",
    "model.widescreen()\n",
    "model.scroll_off()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5078e418",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Load the model, run the baseline and two carbon tax scenarios. Each run is\n",
    "kept under a name in `mpak.keep_solutions`, which the tables below use."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "adf5d067",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Zipped file read:  data\\pak.pcim\n",
      "The feedback variables are not directly connected, so the feedback order is left as found\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "['Baseline', 'Carbon tax 30', 'Carbon tax 60']"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 3,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "mpak, bline = model.modelload('data/pak.pcim', run=True, keep='Baseline')\n",
    "\n",
    "CT30df = bline.upd(\"<2025 2050> PAKGGREVCO2CER PAKGGREVCO2GER PAKGGREVCO2OER = 30\")\n",
    "CT60df = bline.upd(\"<2025 2050> PAKGGREVCO2CER PAKGGREVCO2GER PAKGGREVCO2OER = 60\")\n",
    "\n",
    "_ = mpak(CT30df, 2020, 2050, keep='Carbon tax 30')\n",
    "_ = mpak(CT60df, 2020, 2050, keep='Carbon tax 60')\n",
    "\n",
    "list(mpak.keep_solutions)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9d009128",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "(saving)=\n",
    "## Saving and loading models: `.pcim`, `.pcimz` and `.pcims`\n",
    "\n",
    "A model and its data are saved with `modeldump` and read back with\n",
    "`modelload`. There are now three file formats:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Suffix | Made with | Contains | Use it for |\n",
    "|---|---|---|---|\n",
    "| `.pcim` | `modeldump(file)` | equations, descriptions, data (json, gzipped) | the normal format, readable by all ModelFlow versions |\n",
    "| `.pcimz` | `modeldump(file, large=True)` | the same, with the data in the fast Feather format (zip) | large models (CGE, 100,000+ variables), where `.pcim` is slow; needs `pyarrow` |\n",
    "| `.pcims` | `modeldump(file, data=False)` | the model structure only, no data | sharing a model without its data, or storing the specification |\n",
    "\n",
    "`keep=True` also saves the kept scenarios (`keep_solutions`)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "7e216f7f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Model dumped (feather/zip): saved\\pak_ct.pcimz\n",
      "pak_ct.pcim                   3.82 MB\n",
      "pak_ct.pcimz                  2.46 MB\n",
      "pak_structure.pcims           0.03 MB\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "Path('saved').mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "mpak.modeldump('saved/pak_ct', keep=True)            # -> saved/pak_ct.pcim\n",
    "mpak.modeldump('saved/pak_ct', keep=True, large=True) # -> saved/pak_ct.pcimz (needs pyarrow)\n",
    "mpak.modeldump('saved/pak_structure', data=False)     # -> saved/pak_structure.pcims\n",
    "\n",
    "for f in sorted(Path('saved').iterdir()):\n",
    "    print(f'{f.name:25} {f.stat().st_size/1_000_000:8.2f} MB')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "aa03be4c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "`compact=True` (only with `large=True`) stores the numbers as float32, which\n",
    "halves the file. They are float64 again when the file is loaded.\n",
    "\n",
    "`modelload` finds the format by itself. Without a suffix it tries `.pcimz`,\n",
    "then `.pcim`, then `.pcims`:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "4d97db52",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Feather/zip file read: saved\\pak_ct.pcimz\n",
      "The feedback variables are not directly connected, so the feedback order is left as found\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "['Baseline', 'Carbon tax 30', 'Carbon tax 60']"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 5,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "mpak2, df2 = model.modelload('saved/pak_ct')   # finds saved/pak_ct.pcimz\n",
    "list(mpak2.keep_solutions)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3c4992fc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "A `.pcims` file has no data, so it must be loaded with `run=False`, and the\n",
    "dataframe returned is `None`. Give the model a dataframe yourself, for\n",
    "instance one from another source with the same variables:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "8e9a7369",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Zipped file read:  saved\\pak_structure.pcims\n",
      "The feedback variables are not directly connected, so the feedback order is left as found\n",
      "Structure only model loaded, there is no dataframe in pak_structure.pcims\n",
      "nodata=None, 378 endogenous variables\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "2020    2.627394e+07\n",
       "2021    2.651137e+07\n",
       "2022    2.668514e+07\n",
       "2023    2.696308e+07\n",
       "2024    2.739320e+07\n",
       "2025    2.796323e+07\n",
       "Name: PAKNYGDPMKTPKN, dtype: float64"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 6,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "mstruct, nodata = model.modelload('saved/pak_structure.pcims', run=False)\n",
    "print(f'{nodata=}, {len(mstruct.endogene)} endogenous variables')\n",
    "\n",
    "res = mstruct(bline, 2020, 2050)     # solve with the baseline data from before\n",
    "res.loc[2020:2025, 'PAKNYGDPMKTPKN']"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "83e4f9f2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "File names are no longer case sensitive when loading: `data/PAK.pcim` finds\n",
    "`data/pak.pcim`. Windows never cared, but Linux, the Codespace and\n",
    "JupyterLite do."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "97384fcb",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "(tables)=\n",
    "## Tables with scenarios\n",
    "\n",
    "`model.table()` can now make tables from the kept scenarios, with the\n",
    "`scenarios=` option, as `model.plot()` can.\n",
    "\n",
    "- `scenarios='*'` takes all kept scenarios, in the order they were kept.\n",
    "- Exact names are separated with `|`, for example `'Baseline|Carbon tax 60'`.\n",
    "- Patterns with `*` or `?` are separated with spaces, for example `'Carbon*'`.\n",
    "- For impact datatypes (`difpctlevel`, `diflevel`, `difgrowth`, ...), the\n",
    "  **first** selected scenario is the reference.\n",
    "- Without `scenarios=`, `table` uses basedf and lastdf as before.\n",
    "\n",
    "Levels for all scenarios. Each scenario has a headline row above its rows:"
   ]
  },
  {
