  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e1c8a100",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "(solvers)=\n",
    "## New solvers\n",
    "\n",
    "A new family of solvers is in `modelsolver_ng.py`. They have the suffix\n",
    "`_ng` (next generation) and are chosen with `solver=`. The legacy solvers are\n",
    "still the default, so existing notebooks give the same results.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Solver | Model type | What it does |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| `sim_ng`, `sim1d_ng`, `xgenr_ng` | normalized | the Gauss-Seidel and sweep solvers in the new framework |\n",
    "| `newton_ng` | normalized, implicit and hybrid | Newton per period on the whole model, one solver for all equation types |\n",
    "| `newton_fbmin_ng` | normalized, no leads | Newton only on the minimal feedback set (6 variables in PAK), the rest is solved exactly in topological order. The fastest solver on PAK |\n",
    "| `newtonstack_ng` | all, with leads | stacked Newton over all periods; `split=1` leaves the parts outside the simultaneous core out of the Newton system |\n",
    "| `newtonstack_fbmin_ng` | normalized, with leads | stacked Newton on the stacked feedback set only |\n",
    "\n",
    "Also:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `newton_implicit` now gives the right solution on normalized and hybrid\n",
    "  models. Before, it could give wrong results.\n",
    "- `stats=True` shows the time used, including the time for building the\n",
    "  Jacobian.\n",
    "- The options of a call are remembered for the next call. Use\n",
    "  `reset_options=True` when switching solvers, so options from one solver\n",
    "  don't leak into the next.\n",
    "\n",
    "The chapter *Solving models in ModelFlow* (`solvers/solvers.ipynb`) describes\n",
    "all the solvers and their options.\n",
    "\n",
    "Below, the carbon tax scenario is solved with four solvers. The time and the\n",
    "largest difference from `sim` are shown for each:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "8f83ae2a",
   "metadata": {
    "scrolled": true
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "sim\n",
      "sim_ng\n",
      "newton_ng\n",
      "newton_fbmin_ng\n",
      "sim                  0.152 s   max rel. diff from sim 0.0e+00\n",
      "sim_ng               0.156 s   max rel. diff from sim 0.0e+00\n",
      "newton_ng            0.063 s   max rel. diff from sim 8.0e-05\n",
      "newton_fbmin_ng      0.075 s   max rel. diff from sim 8.3e-05\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import time\n",
    "opts = dict(silent=1, nonlin=4, max_iterations=50)\n",
    "results = {}\n",
    "times = {}\n",
    "for solver in ['sim', 'sim_ng', 'newton_ng', 'newton_fbmin_ng']:\n",
    "    print(solver) \n",
    "    mpak(CT30df, 2020, 2050, solver=solver, reset_options=True, **opts)   # warm up\n",
    "    t0 = time.perf_counter()\n",
    "    results[solver] = mpak(CT30df, 2020, 2050, solver=solver, **opts)\n",
    "    times[solver] = time.perf_counter() - t0\n",
    "\n",
    "endo = sorted(mpak.endogene)\n",
    "ref = results['sim'].loc[2020:2050, endo]\n",
    "for solver, res in results.items():\n",
    "    maxrel = ((res.loc[2020:2050, endo] - ref).abs() / ref.abs().clip(lower=1)).max().max()\n",
    "    print(f'{solver:18} {times[solver]:7.3f} s   max rel. diff from sim {maxrel:.1e}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "72f9a1e4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The differences are within the convergence tolerance. Gauss-Seidel stops\n",
    "when the relative changes are small, Newton when the residuals are small.\n",
    "\n",
    "`stats=True` prints where the time goes:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "63870536",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Setup time (seconds)                 :           0.00\n",
      "Feedback (Newton) variables          :              6\n",
      "DAG core variables                   :             98\n",
      "DAG sweeps (outer iterations)        :            172\n",
      "Inner Newton steps (fb eqs only)     :            141\n",
      "Simulation time (seconds)            :           0.07\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "_ = mpak(CT30df, 2020, 2050, solver='newton_fbmin_ng', stats=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7771be14",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "With `ljit=1` the model is compiled with numba. The first call compiles\n",
    "(about 10 seconds on PAK), and later calls are several times faster. It is\n",
    "worth it when the model is solved many times. It is not available in the\n",
    "browser.\n",
    "\n",
    "```python\n",
    "mpak(CT30df, 2020, 2050, solver='newton_fbmin_ng', ljit=1)\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3adaca5b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "(graphs)=\n",
    "## Graphs without graphviz\n",
    "\n",
    "`model.draw` used to need the graphviz program. Now networkx can draw the\n",
    "graphs too, which also works in the browser:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `engine='svg'` draws an svg. It stays sharp when you zoom, and hovering\n",
    "  over a box or an arrow shows its description and formula.\n",
    "- `engine='mpl'` draws with matplotlib.\n",
    "- `engine='dot'` (the default) uses graphviz. If graphviz fails, ModelFlow\n",
    "  falls back to networkx."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 13,
   "id": "624edcec",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/html": [
