  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d8002116",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "`model.causality(var)` is a new interactive causality graph. Click on a\n",
    "variable to move the graph to it, and press *Back* to go back. It works in\n",
    "JupyterLab, Notebook 7, VS Code and JupyterLite, with neither graphviz nor\n",
    "Dash. It needs `anywidget`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 14,
   "id": "93977df3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json": {
       "model_id": "8233451f5a9e4103943dea3f03b2dc32",
       "version_major": 2,
       "version_minor": 1
      },
      "text/plain": [
       "Interactive causality viewer for PAKNYGDPMKTPKN, run the notebook to use it"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 14,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "mpak.causality('PAKNYGDPMKTPKN', up=1, down=1)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5226dddd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "(jupyter)=\n",
    "## Jupyter Notebook 7 and JupyterLab\n",
    "\n",
    "ModelFlow now works in Jupyter Notebook 7, JupyterLab 4, JupyterLite and VS\n",
    "Code. Notebook 7 is built on JupyterLab, and the classic notebook 6 is no\n",
    "longer developed. What has changed for ModelFlow users:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `model.widescreen()` and `model.scroll_off()` work in Notebook 7,\n",
    "  JupyterLab and JupyterLite. `scroll_off` shows the whole output of a cell\n",
    "  instead of a scroll box.\n",
    "- `model.modelflow_auto()` no longer runs the notebook when it is opened.\n",
    "  That only worked in classic notebook 6. Now it only makes the notebook\n",
    "  wider.\n",
    "- `model.display_toc()` lists the notebooks in a folder as links. They now\n",
    "  open in JupyterLab on Windows too. The root folder name is not shown as a\n",
    "  header any more; use `showroot=True` to show it.\n",
    "- Tab completion (`mpak.<Tab>`) now lists all methods, including the ones\n",
    "  from the mixin classes.\n",
    "- `jupyterlab-myst` is installed with ModelFlow, so markdown cells can use\n",
    "  MyST like a Jupyter Book: note boxes, and diagrams with mermaid. The next\n",
    "  cell is an example."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "914c6966",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    ":::{note}\n",
    "This box is a MyST directive. It renders in JupyterLab and Notebook 7 with\n",
    "`jupyterlab-myst`, and in the Jupyter Book.\n",
    ":::\n",
    "\n",
    "```{mermaid}\n",
    "flowchart LR\n",
    "    A[upd: scenario dataframe] --> B[mpak: solve]\n",
    "    B --> C[keep_solutions]\n",
    "    C --> D[table / plot]\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "91e8a95e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Table of contents of the notebooks in a folder\n",
    "\n",
    "`model.display_toc()` shows a table with links to the notebooks in the current\n",
    "folder and its subfolders. Each row has the notebook's file name, which opens\n",
    "it, and its title, the first heading in the notebook's first cell. A notebook\n",
    "whose name ends in `readme` comes first in its folder. Notebooks whose names\n",
    "start with `test` or `Overview` are left out, unless `all=True`.\n",
    "\n",
    "- `text=` is the header above the table, in markdown.\n",
    "- `folder=` is the folder to start from, default the notebook's own folder.\n",
    "- `nocwd=True` skips the notebooks in the start folder and lists only the\n",
    "  subfolders.\n",
    "- `showroot=True` also shows the name of the start folder as a header.\n",
    "\n",
    "It is handy in the first notebook of a folder with examples. Here it lists the\n",
    "notebooks next to this one."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 15,
   "id": "5659829a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/markdown": [
       "**Notebooks in this folder**"
      ],
      "text/plain": [
       "<IPython.core.display.Markdown object>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "text/html": [
       "<table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;border:none\"><tr><td style=\"text-align:left;padding:2px 24px 2px 2em;white-space:nowrap\"><a href=\"whats_new.ipynb\" target=\"_blank\">whats_new</a></td><td style=\"text-align:left;padding:2px 12px\">New features by example</td></tr></table>"
      ],
      "text/plain": [
       "<IPython.core.display.HTML object>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "mpak.display_toc(text='**Notebooks in this folder**')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c05b2589",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Plain html for RISE slides\n",
    "\n",
    "RISE shows notebooks as slides, but it can't display the ipywidgets Tab and\n",
    "Accordion containers. With `model.plain_html = True`, the result viewer\n",
    "(`mpak['...']`) and `rplot` use plain html tabs and collapsible sections\n",
    "instead. These display anywhere html is shown."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 16,
   "id": "dc450faa",
   "metadata": {},
