   "source": [
    "(widgets)=\n",
    "## Input widgets\n",
    "\n",
    "- Slider operators `%of` and `+%of` (and `%of_impulse`, `+%of_impulse`, for\n",
    "  the first period only). The slider value is a percent of a divisor\n",
    "  variable, typically GDP. The variable is set to that amount, or the amount\n",
    "  is added to it.\n",
    "- `modelinput_shiny.make_app` builds a Shiny web app from the same widget\n",
    "  definitions as the notebook widgets. It also runs in the browser with\n",
    "  Shinylive.\n",
    "- The input widgets now start quickly for models with many variables.\n",
    "\n",
    "`Pakistan/interactive.ipynb` has a full example. Here is a slider for\n",
    "government transfers in percent of GDP:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 18,
   "id": "bd19e168",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json": {
       "model_id": "c866821fd342401eb4591d514309e136",
       "version_major": 2,
       "version_minor": 0
      },
      "text/plain": [
       "VBox(children=(VBox(children=(HBox(children=(Label(value='Government expenditure, % of GDP', layout=Layout(wid…"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from modelwidget_input import make_widget, updatewidget\n",
    "\n",
    "gov_slidedef = ['slide', {\n",
    "    'heading': 'Government expenditure, % of GDP',\n",
    "    'content': {\n",
    "        'Transfers to households': {'var': 'PAKGGEXPTRNSCN_X', 'value': 0.0, 'min': -2.0, 'max': 2.0,\n",
    "                                    'step': 0.1, 'op': '+%of', 'divisor': 'PAKNYGDPMKTPCN'},\n",
    "    }\n",
    "}]\n",
    "\n",
    "ui = updatewidget(mpak, make_widget(gov_slidedef), varpat='PAKNYGDPMKTPKN PAKNYGDPMKTPCN')\n",
    "ui"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "68e4a71a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "(largemodels)=\n",
    "## Large models: other factorizations, fast loading, stored derivatives\n",
    "\n",
    "A stacked Newton solve (`newtonstack_ng`) of a large forward-looking model ends in\n",
    "one very large linear system: all equations times all periods. The Danish model\n",
    "MAKRO (DREAM), translated to ModelFlow, has 20,474 equations and is solved for\n",
    "100 years in one system with 1.5 million unknowns. SuperLU, the default, gives up\n",
    "on a system that size. The option `factorizer=` chooses another method:\n",
    "\n",
    "| `factorizer=` | Method | Needs |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| `None`, `'superlu'` | SuperLU through scipy (the default), ordering with `permc_spec=` | |\n",
    "| `'umfpack'` | UMFPACK | `cvxopt` |\n",
    "| `'pardiso'` | LU with MKL PARDISO, multi-threaded | `pypardiso` |\n",
    "| `'normal'` | the Newton step through the normal equations $J'J x = J'b$ with a PARDISO Cholesky factorization, refined against $J$. The fastest on a large stacked system | `pypardiso` |\n",
    "| `'mumps'` | LU with MUMPS, in this process or in a helper process | `python-mumps` |\n",
    "| a function | `f(J)` returns a function `solve(b)` | |\n",
    "\n",
    "The option works for `newton_ng` and `newtonstack_ng`. The methods check their\n",
    "own answer: when the linear solve is inaccurate, they raise an error instead of\n",
    "giving Newton a wrong step. `'normal'` and `'pardiso'` are for large, well\n",
    "conditioned systems. On FRB/US they fail with a clear message, so SuperLU stays\n",
    "the default.\n",
    "\n",
    "This is how MAKRO is solved (not run here, the model is not public):\n",
    "\n",
    "```python\n",
    "mmakro, baseline = model.modelload('makro26_baseline.pcimz')\n",
    "result = mmakro(scenario, 2030, 2129, solver='newtonstack_ng',\n",
    "                forcenum=False, factorizer='normal')\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Three other changes make a model of that size practical:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **`straight=True`** in `model(...)` and `modelload(...)` keeps the equations in\n",
    "  the order of the file and skips the analysis of the simultaneous structure.\n",
    "  The stacked Newton solvers don't use it, and on MAKRO the search for\n",
    "  feedback variables took two minutes of a load. `modeldump` stores the choice,\n",
    "  so the model loads the same way next time (1.5 seconds).\n",
    "- **Stored derivatives.** The Newton solvers keep the symbolic derivatives on\n",
    "  the model (`model.diff_expressions`). `modeldump(file, derivatives=True)`\n",
    "  saves them in the file, and a later session skips the differentiation, which\n",
    "  was two minutes of the first stacked solve.\n",
    "- **The stacked Jacobian is filled from a plan** (coming in the next release).\n",
    "  The sparsity pattern is made once, and a rebuild only places the new values.\n",
    "  On MAKRO a rebuild of the matrix went from 19 seconds to 3 seconds.\n",
    "  `stackfill='melt'` gives the former fill.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0b4fbb8e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "(ode)=\n",
    "## Differential equations: `modelode`\n",
    "\n",
    "ModelFlow solves difference equations, one dataframe row per period. The new\n",
    "module `modelode` lets you write a model in continuous time, as derivatives,\n",
    "and generates the equations of a Runge-Kutta step. Each row is then one time\n",
    "step, and the ordinary solver runs it. It can be used for physics, epidemics\n",
    "(SIR), chemical kinetics and growth models in continuous time.\n",
    "\n",
    "An equation with the option `<ODE>` gives a derivative:\n",
    "`FRML <ODE> S = f $` means $\\frac{dS}{dt} = f$. `ode_transform` returns the\n",
    "equations of the chosen method: `euler`, `heun`, `midpoint`, `ralston` or `rk4`\n",
    "(the default), or your own Butcher tableau. The time step is a column in the\n",
    "dataframe (`DT`), so it can change from row to row.\n",
    "\n",
    "Here is an epidemic model (SIR). `report=True` shows how each equation was read:\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "23bff59a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/html": [
       "<table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;margin:4px 0\">\n",
       "<tr><th style=\"border:1px solid #999;padding:3px 8px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">variable</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #999;padding:3px 8px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">class</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #999;padding:3px 8px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">derivative / expression</th></tr>\n",
       "<tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #999;padding:3px 8px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;font-family:monospace;white-space:nowrap\">S</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #999;padding:3px 8px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">state</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #999;padding:3px 8px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;font-family:monospace;white-space:nowrap\">-INFECTION_RATE*S*I/N</td></tr>\n",
       "<tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #999;padding:3px 8px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;font-family:monospace;white-space:nowrap\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #999;padding:3px 8px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">state</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #999;padding:3px 8px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;font-family:monospace;white-space:nowrap\">INFECTION_RATE*S*I/N-RECOVERY_RATE*I</td></tr>\n",
       "<tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #999;padding:3px 8px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;font-family:monospace;white-space:nowrap\">R</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #999;padding:3px 8px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">state</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #999;padding:3px 8px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;font-family:monospace;white-space:nowrap\">RECOVERY_RATE*I</td></tr>\n",
       "<tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #999;padding:3px 8px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;font-family:monospace;white-space:nowrap\">N</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #999;padding:3px 8px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">aux</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #999;padding:3px 8px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;font-family:monospace;white-space:nowrap\">S + I + R</td></tr>\n",
       "</table>\n",
       "<p><b>Exogenous:</b> <code>INFECTION_RATE</code>, <code>RECOVERY_RATE</code> &nbsp; <b>Step:</b> <code>DT</code> &nbsp; <b>Method:</b> rk4</p>\n",
       "<p><i>state</i>: integrated, the column is its derivative; <i>aux</i>: needed by a derivative, recomputed at every stage; <i>report</i>: needed by no derivative, computed once at the end of the step.</p>"
      ],
      "text/markdown": [
       "| variable | class | derivative / expression |\n",
       "|:--|:--|:--|\n",
       "| `S` | state | `-INFECTION_RATE*S*I/N` |\n",
       "| `I` | state | `INFECTION_RATE*S*I/N-RECOVERY_RATE*I` |\n",
       "| `R` | state | `RECOVERY_RATE*I` |\n",
       "| `N` | aux | `S + I + R` |\n",
       "\n",
       "**Exogenous:** `INFECTION_RATE`, `RECOVERY_RATE` &nbsp; **Step:** `DT` &nbsp; **Method:** rk4\n",
       "\n",
       "*state*: integrated, the column is its derivative; *aux*: needed by a derivative, recomputed at every stage; *report*: needed by no derivative, computed once at the end of the step."
      ],
      "text/plain": [
       "| variable | class | derivative / expression |\n",
       "|:--|:--|:--|\n",
       "| `S` | state | `-INFECTION_RATE*S*I/N` |\n",
       "| `I` | state | `INFECTION_RATE*S*I/N-RECOVERY_RATE*I` |\n",
       "| `R` | state | `RECOVERY_RATE*I` |\n",
       "| `N` | aux | `S + I + R` |\n",
       "\n",
       "**Exogenous:** `INFECTION_RATE`, `RECOVERY_RATE` &nbsp; **Step:** `DT` &nbsp; **Method:** rk4\n",
       "\n",
       "*state*: integrated, the column is its derivative; *aux*: needed by a derivative, recomputed at every stage; *report*: needed by no derivative, computed once at the end of the step."
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "32 equations generated from 4\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from modelode import ode_transform\n",
    "\n",
    "sir = '''\n",
    "FRML <ODE> S = -INFECTION_RATE*S*I/N                   $\n",
    "FRML <ODE> I = INFECTION_RATE*S*I/N - RECOVERY_RATE*I $\n",
    "FRML <ODE> R = RECOVERY_RATE*I                         $\n",
    "FRML <>    N = S + I + R                               $\n",
    "'''\n",
    "msir = model(ode_transform(sir, method='rk4', report=True), modelname='SIR, RK4')\n",
    "print(len(msir.endogene), 'equations generated from 4')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c3a1f957",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Row 0 of the dataframe holds the starting state, and the model is solved\n",
    "from row 1. Here one row is a quarter of a day:\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a02ccf24",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x350 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "days, dt = 120, 0.25\n",
    "sirdf = pd.DataFrame(0.0, index=range(int(days/dt) + 1), columns=sorted(msir.allvar))\n",
    "sirdf['DT'], sirdf['INFECTION_RATE'], sirdf['RECOVERY_RATE'] = dt, 0.3, 0.1\n",
    "sirdf.loc[0, ['S', 'I', 'R', 'N']] = 999.0, 1.0, 0.0, 1000.0\n",
    "\n",
    "sirres = msir(sirdf, 1, sirdf.index[-1], silent=1)\n",
    "ax = sirres[['S', 'I', 'R']].set_index(sirres.index*dt).plot(\n",
    "        title='SIR model, Runge-Kutta 4', xlabel='days', figsize=(8, 3.5))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "23a03028",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### N-body models\n",
    "\n",
    "`ode_makemodel` reads a documented markdown model with lists and `doable`\n",
    "lines, like `Makemodel`. In such a model `NO{list}` means *all the other\n",
    "elements* of the list, which is what gravity needs: each body is pulled by all\n",
    "the others. `modelode` comes with a ready N-body template and helpers.\n",
    "\n",
    "The Sun, the Earth and Jupiter in two dimensions, with units of AU, days and\n",
    "solar masses. One row is one day:\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f8f7f30e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "117 equations, 4383 steps, relative change in total energy 5.0e-11\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from modelode import nbody_makemodel, make_df, zero_momentum, energy, pos, G_AU_DAY\n",
    "\n",
    "bodies = ['SUN', 'EARTH', 'JUPITER']\n",
    "mbody, mm = nbody_makemodel(bodies, dims=2, method='rk4')\n",
    "\n",
    "masses = {'SUN': 1.0, 'EARTH': 3.003e-6, 'JUPITER': 9.546e-4}             # solar masses\n",
    "pos0 = {'SUN': (0, 0), 'EARTH': (1.0, 0), 'JUPITER': (5.2, 0)}            # AU\n",
    "vel0 = zero_momentum(bodies, masses,                                      # AU per day\n",
    "                     {'SUN': (0, 0), 'EARTH': (0, 0.0172), 'JUPITER': (0, 0.00754)}, 'SUN')\n",
    "bodydf = make_df(mbody, bodies, masses, pos0, vel0, G_AU_DAY, dt=1.0, t_max=12*365.25)\n",
    "\n",
    "orbits = mbody(bodydf, 1, bodydf.index[-1], silent=1)\n",
    "e = energy(orbits, bodies, masses, G_AU_DAY, dims=2)\n",
    "print(f'{len(mbody.endogene)} equations, {len(orbits) - 1} steps, '\n",
    "      f'relative change in total energy {abs(e.iloc[-1]/e.iloc[0] - 1):.1e}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7ff8a537",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 500x500 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(5, 5))\n",
    "for body in bodies:\n",
    "    ax.plot(orbits[pos(body, 'X')], orbits[pos(body, 'Y')], label=body.capitalize())\n",
    "ax.set(aspect='equal', xlabel='AU', ylabel='AU', title='12 years, one step per day')\n",
    "ax.legend();"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1e13d233",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "`mm.render` shows the documented model the equations were made from. The\n",
    "method has limits: no delays (lags of 2 or more), no leads, and the equations\n",
    "of a step must not be simultaneous.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "064751ab",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "(montecarlo)=\n",
    "## Monte Carlo simulation: `modelmontecarlo`\n",
    "\n",
    ":::{note}\n",
    "`modelmontecarlo` is not in the released ModelFlow yet (version 2.94). This\n",
    "section shows what is coming; the cells can't be run with a released version.\n",
    ":::\n",
    "\n",
    "`modelmontecarlo.montecarlo` draws shocks for chosen exogenous variables,\n",
    "solves the model once for each draw and collects the chosen variables. The\n",
    "result has fan charts, tables of quantiles and probabilities of any condition\n",
    "on the variables.\n",
    "\n",
    "Below, the uncertainty is in four behavioural equations of the Pakistan model:\n",
    "shocks to the add factors of private consumption, private investment, exports\n",
    "and imports. `shocks` gives the standard deviation of each. With\n",
    "`draw='each'` there is a new shock every year.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "bfcb9c78",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "200 draws solved in 18.4 s, 0 failed\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "McResult(pak: 200 draws, 200 usable, 0 failed, 4 variables)"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 9,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import modelmontecarlo as mc\n",
    "\n",
    "mcres = mc.montecarlo(\n",
    "    mpak, bline, 2025, 2050,\n",
    "    shocks={'PAKNECONPRVTKN_A': 0.01,     # private consumption\n",
    "            'PAKNEGDIFPRVKN_A': 0.002,    # private investment\n",
    "            'PAKNEEXPGNFSKN_A': 0.03,     # exports\n",
    "            'PAKNEIMPGNFSKN_A': 0.02},    # imports\n",
    "    shock_defaults={'draw': 'each'},\n",
    "    n=200, method='antithetic', seed=2026,\n",
    "    keep_variables='PAKNYGDPMKTPKN PAKNECONPRVTKN PAKNYGDPMKTPCN PAKGGDBTTOTLCN',\n",
    "    name='pak', keep=False, solver='sim_ng', progress=False)\n",
    "mcres"
   ]
  },
