  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c19b68b0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The module also has:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Shocks**: added, in percent, to the growth rate or in logs; one shock in\n",
    "  the first period, over the whole horizon or a new one each period; normal, t\n",
    "  and lognormal distributions; a correlation matrix.\n",
    "- **Estimation**: standard deviations, correlations and AR(1) coefficients\n",
    "  estimated from history (`estimate=`), or whole historical periods drawn again\n",
    "  (bootstrap).\n",
    "- **Better draws**: antithetic, Latin hypercube and Sobol sampling, and common\n",
    "  draws to compare two policies (`common_draws=`, `impact`).\n",
    "- **Forward-looking models**: `information='surprise'` reveals the shocks\n",
    "  period by period.\n",
    "- **Conditional draws**: `condition=` fixes some shocks and draws the others\n",
    "  given them, a stress scenario with a distribution around it.\n",
    "- **Analysis**: the worst draws and what drove them (`tail`, `tail_profile`),\n",
    "  `sensitivity`, and how many draws a given precision needs.\n",
    "- **Parallel runs**: `executor=8` solves the draws in 8 processes.\n",
    "- **A widget**: `mc.gui(...)` sets up and runs a simulation in the notebook.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "45b09f16",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "(claude)=\n",
    "## ModelFlow with Claude: plugins, skills and an MCP server\n",
    "\n",
    "The repository [modelflow-skill](https://github.com/IbHansen/modelflow-skill)\n",
    "has plugins for [Claude Code](https://code.claude.com/docs). A plugin is a set\n",
    "of *skills*: instructions Claude reads when a task calls for them, so it knows\n",
    "how ModelFlow is used. There is one plugin for each kind of user:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Plugin | For | Skills on |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| `modelflow-user` | people who run existing models | installing, loading a model, variable names (MFMod, FRB/US, MAKRO), scenarios, results, attribution, reports, ODE simulations and animations |\n",
    "| `modelflow-modeller` | people who build and maintain models | the equation language, FRML options, naming, normalization, Makemodel, ODE models, estimation, data, model structure, solvers, import from other systems, debugging; a `model-reviewer` agent |\n",
    "| `modelflow-dev` | developers of ModelFlow | architecture, conventions, design notes, the `_ng` solvers, code generation, regression tests |\n",
    "\n",
    "Some skills are commands: `/mf-scenario` turns a policy described in words into\n",
    "a scenario, `/mf-compare` compares scenarios, `/mf-explain` explains a\n",
    "variable, `/mf-check-model` reports on a model and `/mf-explain-error` explains\n",
    "an error message.\n",
    "\n",
    "### The MCP server\n",
    "\n",
    "`modelflow-user` also has an MCP server. With it Claude does not only write\n",
    "code for you to run. It loads a model in a Python process of its own, runs\n",
    "scenarios and reads the results, so you can ask *\"what happens to GDP and\n",
    "emissions in Pakistan with a carbon tax of 30?\"* and get the answer with a\n",
    "table. The tools are:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Tool | What it does |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| `load_model`, `list_models` | load a `.pcim` file, list the loaded models |\n",
    "| `find_variables`, `explain_variable` | search names and descriptions, show the equation and what drives a variable |\n",
    "| `run_scenario` | run a scenario written as `upd` lines |\n",
    "| `show_results` | levels and differences from the baseline |\n",
    "| `environment_status`, `list_environments`, `select_environment` | choose the conda environment ModelFlow runs in |\n",
    "\n",
    "The server runs ModelFlow in the conda environment `modelflow`, which needs\n",
    "the package `mcp`.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Installing\n",
    "\n",
    "In a terminal on Windows, with Git and Miniforge installed:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "conda create -n modelflow -c ibh -c conda-forge modelflow mcp\n",
    "claude plugin marketplace add IbHansen/modelflow-skill\n",
    "claude plugin install modelflow-user@modelflow\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Add `modelflow-modeller@modelflow` and `modelflow-dev@modelflow` the same way.\n",
    "The README of the repository has the other routes: a clone with `setup.cmd`,\n",
    "and the MCP server alone for Claude Desktop.\n",
    "\n",
    ":::{warning}\n",
    "The plugins and the MCP server are experimental and will change. Check what\n",
    "Claude tells you against ModelFlow itself.\n",
    ":::\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ebbec7b1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "(fitted)=\n",
    "## Fitted values of estimated equations\n",
    "\n",
    "An equation estimated in `Makemodel` (with `<est=...>` in its options) is often\n",
    "written for a transformation of the variable, here `DLOG(CON)` in an error\n",
    "correction model of private consumption. The actual and fitted values the\n",
    "estimator works with, `af_df` and `residuals_df`, are then growth rates.\n",
    "`af_level_df` gives them for the variable itself: the estimated equation solved\n",
    "for `CON` and evaluated on the data, with the actual lags (a one-step fit).\n",
    "Its columns are prefixed with the variable name, so frames of several\n",
    "equations can be joined side by side.\n",
    "\n",
    "The data is consumption and GDP from the World Bank model for Nepal. With\n",
    "`type_input='single'` the text is one equation, which may run over several\n",
    "lines."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "6a5f8ae5",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-11-17T13:26:52.756010Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-11-17T13:26:52.755839Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-11-17T13:26:55.719199Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-11-17T13:26:55.718410Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
